# Normalize all text files to LF on checkout and commit, regardless of a
# given contributor's core.autocrlf setting.
#
# Without this, Windows checkouts with core.autocrlf=true let git rewrite
# committed LF files to CRLF on disk on every checkout/commit -- even when
# the file's actual content hasn't changed. That silent rewrite bumps the
# file's mtime, which has caused two separate false positives in this repo:
#   - scripts/check-deps.sh comparing package-lock.json's mtime against
#     node_modules/.package-lock.json to detect a stale install; a CRLF-only
#     rewrite looks identical to a real dependency change to that check.
#   - the pre-push hook's `npm run check-format` (prettier --check) failing
#     on files nobody touched in the current branch, because Windows
#     re-normalized them to CRLF while prettier expects LF.
# Pinning everything to LF here removes the churn at the source instead of
# working around it in each affected script.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit binary types -- git's own heuristic already detects these, but
# being explicit avoids any risk of eol=lf accidentally corrupting them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
